# Improved TAM Parameter List for AU-Tum Site
# Version 2 - Robust configuration
#
# Key improvements:
# 1. Reduced parameter count to address identifiability (removed perfectly correlated parameters)
# 2. Tightened ranges to avoid zero GPP combinations
# 3. Focused on most influential parameters from sensitivity analysis
# 4. Added leaf parameters to help reach observed GPP range (2500-4500 gC/m²/year)
#
# Format: parameter_name distribution_type min max
# distribution_type: 5 = uniform
#
# TAM Framework: Transport (T), Absorptive (A), Mycorrhizal (M) root traits
# ==================================================================================

# ROOT C:N RATIOS (Most influential parameters: 4-6% impact on GPP)
# Keep all three root types to preserve TAM framework
# CRITICAL: Low C:N causes zero GPP by sequestering N in roots
# Analysis shows: Need C:N > 95-160 to avoid zero GPP
froottcn 5 100 160   # Transport root C:N (was 20-184, min raised from 20→100)
frootacn 5 70 110    # Absorptive root C:N (was 11-119, min raised from 11→70)
frootmcn 5 13 22     # Mycorrhizal root C:N (was 7-25, narrowed safe range)

# ROOT C:P RATIOS
# REMOVED frootacp and frootmcp (perfectly correlated with froottcp, <1% GPP impact)
# Keep only transport CP as representative
froottcp 5 450 900   # Transport root C:P (was 375-1125, tightened to mid-range)

# ROOT LONGEVITY (Moderate influence: 2-3% impact on GPP)
# CRITICAL: Long absorptive roots + high N = zero GPP (N sequestration)
# Analysis shows: froota_long > 1.23 causes zero GPP
froott_long 5 4 8    # Transport root longevity (years) (was 3-10, avoid very short)
froota_long 5 0.6 1.2 # Absorptive root longevity (years) (was 0.5-4, max reduced 4→1.2)
frootm_long 5 0.3 0.7 # Mycorrhizal root longevity (years) (was 0.13-1, narrowed)

# ROOT CHEMISTRY FRACTIONS
# Consolidated to most influential only
frt_flab 5 0.15 0.30  # Transport root labile fraction (was 0.1-0.35, tightened)
fra_flab 5 0.15 0.30  # Absorptive root labile fraction (was 0.1-0.35, tightened)
# REMOVED all fcel parameters (minimal impact <1%)

# ROOT-LEAF ALLOCATION (Critical for GPP!)
# These control carbon allocation between roots and leaves
# Tightened to ensure sufficient leaf allocation for photosynthesis
froott_leaf 5 0.10 0.30  # Transport root to leaf allocation (was 0.05-0.4, avoid too low)
froota_leaf 5 0.25 0.50  # Absorptive root to leaf allocation (was 0.2-0.6, mid-range)

# ADDED: LEAF PARAMETERS to help reach observed GPP range
# These couple with TAM root nutrient uptake to determine photosynthetic capacity
leafcn 5 25 35       # Leaf C:N ratio (lower = more N per leaf = higher vcmax)
slatop 5 0.008 0.015 # Specific leaf area (m²/gC) (higher = more leaf area per C)

# ==================================================================================
# PARAMETER COUNT: 13 (down from 17)
#
# Removed (5 parameters):
#   - frootacp, frootmcp (correlated with froottcp)
#   - frt_fcel, fra_fcel, frm_fcel (minimal impact)
#   - frm_flab (consolidated)
#
# Added (1 parameter):
#   - leafcn, slatop (needed to reach realistic GPP)
#
# ZERO GPP PREVENTION (Based on analysis of 1000-member ensemble):
#   Original ensemble: 342/1000 (34.2%) produced zero GPP
#   Root cause: Low root C:N + Long absorptive roots = N sequestration in roots
#
#   Key fixes:
#   1. froottcn min: 20 → 100 (avoid N-luxury roots)
#   2. frootacn min: 11 → 70 (avoid N-luxury roots)
#   3. froota_long max: 4 → 1.2 (avoid long-lived N-rich roots)
#
#   Expected result: <5% zero GPP cases (down from 34%)
#
# ENSEMBLE SIZE RECOMMENDATION: 1000 samples minimum
#   - With 13 parameters, need ~75-100 samples per parameter for robust surrogates
#   - Target R² > 0.90 for all variables
#
# NOTES:
# - CN ratios kept separate for T/A/M roots despite correlation (preserves TAM structure)
# - Use informative priors in MCMC if correlation persists
# - leafcn and slatop couple root nutrient supply to leaf photosynthesis
# - These ranges based on empirical analysis: analyze_zero_gpp.py
# ==================================================================================
